  "notesHtml": "<ol>\n          <li>(a) One month of a 24-month policy has elapsed: $8,424 &#x00f7; 24 = $351.</li>\n          <li>(b) Supplies used = $3,960 &#x2212; $1,845 = $2,115.</li>\n          <li>(c) Monthly depreciation = $16,608 &#x00f7; 96 months = $173.</li>\n          <li>(d) One of six months' rent has now been earned: $14,400 &#x00f7; 6 = $2,400 (matches the $2,400/month rate given).</li>\n          <li>(e) Salaries earned but unpaid is accrued expense: debit the expense, credit a payable.</li>\n        </ol>\n        <button class=\"answer-toggle\" aria-expanded=\"false\">Answer <span class=\"chev\">&#x2304;</span></button>\n        <div class=\"answer-reveal\">\n          <ol>\n            <li><span class=\"ans-part\">a.</span> Debit Insurance Expense $351; Credit Prepaid Insurance $351.</li>\n            <li><span class=\"ans-part\">b.</span> Debit Supplies Expense $2,115; Credit Supplies $2,115.</li>\n            <li><span class=\"ans-part\">c.</span> Debit Depreciation Expense $173; Credit Accumulated Depreciation $173.</li>\n            <li><span class=\"ans-part\">d.</span> Debit Unearned Rent Revenue $2,400; Credit Rent Revenue $2,400.</li>\n            <li><span class=\"ans-part\">e.</span> Debit Salaries Expense $1,296; Credit Salaries Payable $1,296.</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>"
